  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA, multi-profile, PCA, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc, a substantial +10.6% gain over config_001 (single-profile, 0.485), confirming that multi-profile aggregation is a high-impact design choice. However, we only have one data point on aggregation method (avgpool). Uncertainty: It is unclear whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer) further improves over simple averaging, which would change the aggregation choice for all downstream multimodal experiments. This experiment (config_003) isolates exactly one variable—aggregation method (transformer vs avgpool)—while holding RNA encoder (PCA n2000), profile setting (multi), and modality (RNA-only) constant, making it a clean A/B comparison with config_002. If transformer significantly outperforms avgpool, it signals that learned aggregation is worth pursuing across encoders and modalities; if it is comparable, avgpool is sufficient and budget is better spent exploring encoder choice or multimodal fusion. Under a limited budget, resolving this binary design question with a controlled comparison is more informative than jumping to a less certain multimodal or new-encoder configuration."
